Ukraine's attack on the Kerch Bridge damaged a key transportation link between occupied Crimea and Russia. Estonian Defense Forces Lt. Col. Taavi Liias says that if Ukraine succeeds in disabling the rail connection as well, it could significantly complicate Russian military logistics on the southern front.
Last week's most striking development in the war was the destruction of the road section of the Kerch Bridge connecting occupied Crimea and Russia, along with damage to the railway bridge. How did the Ukrainians pull this off? The bridge is a highly symbolic structure for Russia, in some ways a symbol of the occupation itself. Was this operation prepared for quite a long time?
